comments.content:
Just 1. 
We likely will only use for three months. Maybe in the future we can renew and do a separate campaign but I already told them we are done after three months to take time to evaluate results. 
@gentlementlegen i think we can disable priority gating on this repository. There's no pulls to review so it's less burdensome to review.

@minhyeong112 something I've been thinking about for a while, but I think that we have much greater success if we put together
educational materials highlighting the system features, and its benefits, together.
Then when you send out all this messaging, you can also link the materials so they can peruse and get a better understanding of what exactly were trying to get them to use

@0x4007 FYI - I like their data - it's pretty exclusive and it's all about Web3. We definitely can leverage it. 
@minhyeong112 launched his first campaign on community managers, so let's see where those gonna land and let's discuss CxO campaigns and whether we are going to do that in multi-channel manner (i strongly recommend that), or should we just run telegram campaigns (in case we will see 40%+ response rate, why would we need anything else). 
We need to do more tests to see how good it is in terms of revealing TGs for VCs and other organizations. 
Overall, this tool definitely could be a solution for telegram outreach.
